1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:07,657
Imagine giving someone a real share of NVIDIA, Apple, or Tesla, as easily as sending a text message.

2
00:00:07,977 --> 00:00:08,732
This is Convey.

3
00:00:09,582 --> 00:00:13,553
Tokenized stocks, called xStocks, now live on X Layer.

4
00:00:13,873 --> 00:00:15,731
But receiving one today is hard.

5
00:00:16,051 --> 00:00:22,680
Your friend needs a crypto wallet, a seed phrase, the right network, and gas tokens, before they can even accept the gift.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,463
Most people give up right there.

7
00:00:25,313 --> 00:00:28,982
Convey removes every one of those steps for the person receiving the gift.

8
00:00:29,302 --> 00:00:31,485
The sender pays from their OKX Wallet.

9
00:00:31,805 --> 00:00:35,636
The recipient simply opens a link, and confirms with their fingerprint.

10
00:00:35,956 --> 00:00:40,496
The stock lands in their own OKX Smart Wallet, and they never pay any gas.

11
00:00:40,816 --> 00:00:46,267
No custody, and no mock data. Every contract you'll see is live on X Layer mainnet.

12
00:00:47,117 --> 00:00:50,496
Let's walk through it, end to end, starting with the sender.

13
00:00:50,816 --> 00:00:55,030
They connect OKX Wallet, and Convey switches it to X Layer automatically.

14
00:00:55,350 --> 00:01:00,412
They choose an xStock, shown with its live price, enter an amount, and add a personal note.

15
00:01:00,732 --> 00:01:07,779
One transaction locks the stock in Convey's escrow, together with a tiny OKB reserve that will pay the recipient's gas.

16
00:01:08,099 --> 00:01:10,723
Convey then creates a private gift link.

17
00:01:11,573 --> 00:01:13,500
That link is protected by design.

18
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:16,595
It carries a one-time key that never goes on chain.

19
00:01:16,915 --> 00:01:24,862
At claim time, the key signs for one specific account. So even if someone sees the claim, they can't redirect the gift to themselves.

20
00:01:25,712 --> 00:01:30,560
Now, the recipient, on their phone. This is a real claim, on X Layer mainnet.

21
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:34,955
They open the link, and see exactly what they received, valued live.

22
00:01:35,275 --> 00:01:38,962
One tap creates a passkey. There is no seed phrase to write down.

23
00:01:39,282 --> 00:01:46,585
Convey's gateway creates their smart wallet, the paymaster sponsors the gas, and our own OKBund bundler submits the transaction.

24
00:01:46,905 --> 00:01:50,626
Confirmed, in about twenty seconds. The recipient paid nothing.

25
00:01:51,476 --> 00:02:00,149
From here, the stock is theirs. They can keep it, cash it out to USDT0 at a live quote, or move it anywhere. All gasless.

26
00:02:00,999 --> 00:02:03,391
Convey is also built for AI agents.

27
00:02:03,711 --> 00:02:13,115
Through our MCP server, an agent like Claude, or an OKX AI agent, can check live xStock prices, gift a stock to someone, and track its status.

28
00:02:13,435 --> 00:02:17,777
It always asks the user before spending, and never exceeds the cap you set.

29
00:02:18,627 --> 00:02:23,306
Agents can also gift on a schedule, like one share of Apple, every month.

30
00:02:23,626 --> 00:02:33,013
You approve the plan once. Your OKX Smart Wallet adds the agent as a restricted owner, with an on-chain budget it cannot exceed, even if its key leaks.

31
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:40,805
We proved this on mainnet. Two gifts within the budget. A third one, blocked by the wallet. And then, the agent revoked.

32
00:02:41,655 --> 00:02:45,231
Convey is built on the OKX stack, from end to end.

33
00:02:45,551 --> 00:02:55,560
X Layer for settlement. OKX Wallet for senders. xStocks as the assets. The OKX Smart Wallet for recipients. And OKBund as our bundler.

34
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:59,226
Convey. Gift real stocks, in one link.

35
00:02:59,546 --> 00:03:01,798
Live now at conveyapp.site

